l consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "74f1533d-9e2a-4979-bcbf-7b91ba78dc29", "active": true, "entity_id": "70bada9b-e142-4aa2-897b-24ac5ff734a7", "source_id": "844f5cba-66a7-4781-bb9b-ac2f5ef290ac", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "waterproof_flat_roof — Existing-membrane compatibility must be verified against the selected kit rather than assumed.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "The EAD treats liquid-applied roof waterproofing as a kit assessed for defined substrates/components and intended use.", "relevant_section_page": "§1.1 scope and kit concept"}, {"id": "7c019b77-a279-4cd9-89ec-973d5c310d94", "active": true, "entity_id": "70e370b2-45bd-4d53-8006-abfd1599ee1b", "source_id": "d3d86175-0a94-4a12-93e0-3dae713325c9", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_wood_bare — General wood-finishing behaviour; exact product system remains Layer B.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "The USDA Wood Handbook finishing chapter discusses selection of finishes in relation to wood, exposure, moisture and intended service.", "relevant_section_page": "Chapter 16 — Finishing wood"}, {"id": "09855eed-5a5b-404c-a21c-e76a5edeea19", "active": true, "entity_id": "71070e5a-8c50-453b-badf-ef5a9ffe072b", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_repaint_sound — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "0bccac04-8cf8-403f-bbfe-36a6f9e48aa0", "active": true, "entity_id": "71de5dfe-f290-4d0e-9a25-637f736339ac", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "repair_damaged_plaster — Exact drying/cure time remains product-specific.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Wall-repair guidance requires patching compounds to dry before sanding and subsequent finishing steps.", "relevant_section_page": "Repairing small/larger holes — drying before sanding/finishing"}, {"id": "6c1caafa-77ee-42ae-9f68-14ef6554b5d3", "active": true, "entity_id": "7430ea04-36f6-4929-959a-5642662ffe01", "source_id": "2c3bac1e-4007-42c5-afb0-8bff6506b469", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "insulation_external_etics — EU ETICS system principle.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "The EAD scope treats ETICS as a kit applied on site rather than an arbitrary set of independently selected products.", "relevant_section_page": "§1.1 scope and ETICS components"}, {"id": "a2f37500-a356-4fff-a16e-745f7fdc5252", "active": true, "entity_id": "7d843ff2-cc37-41ae-928b-8a6ff41c54b2", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "insulation_external_etics — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "25801a0f-6a1f-480a-9ee4-3eb21267ba3a", "active": true, "entity_id": "821139c0-b005-4a1b-ab69-8f2e98964031", "source_id": "fa2cc5eb-db76-43dc-afe1-19f2d0a7c786", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_exterior_hairline_cracks — Used as conservative diagnostic guidance; not Greek structural law.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Government building-maintenance guidance treats cracking and movement as conditions that may require monitoring and professional investigation rather than diagnosis from appearance alone.", "relevant_section_page": "Foundation movement / progressive cracking"}, {"id": "c05cc559-267d-4424-89b9-65d1705bd56f", "active": true, "entity_id": "8771d0d8-8cf4-48b0-8448-e8e6a40f94ae", "source_id": "fa2cc5eb-db76-43dc-afe1-19f2d0a7c786", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "repair_hairline_wall_crack — Supports a stability screen before treating a crack as cosmetic.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Government building-maintenance guidance distinguishes progressive movement/cracking as a condition for monitoring and professional advice.", "relevant_section_page": "Progressive cracking / professional advice"}, {"id": "9615ae39-3ad8-45f8-a084-5c8e52aa3a08", "active": true, "entity_id": "893040b6-966c-445a-9f91-9486da80bf34", "source_id": "d41a5be3-5b6c-4d4e-a654-060b263bbafe", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_exterior_hairline_cracks — Supports treating crack-bridging as a declared/tested coating-system property, not a generic assumption.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "EN 1062-7 is specifically a method for determining crack-bridging properties of coating materials and systems for exterior masonry and concrete.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope/title"}, {"id": "1918f5a4-88fe-461d-97f5-55162761a0aa", "active": true, "entity_id": "8c5fda17-ce4d-436d-a841-66f3da8b1abe", "source_id": "7983b9f3-8943-412e-93ca-3212b56b2e14", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_mould_damp — Supports source-first moisture management rather than cosmetic coating alone.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "WHO guidance identifies prevention and minimisation of persistent dampness and microbial growth as the central control approach.", "relevant_section_page": "Overview and recommendations"}, {"id": "8ecbb502-9513-4d5d-ae3a-8286f9625e0b", "active": true, "entity_id": "9964c136-0d87-4719-86f6-0df012e0a3f8", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_mould_damp — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "7e8bf8b7-b5db-431d-bb3e-0f23054ab0fe", "active": true, "entity_id": "9ff6cbbd-2e14-45e6-993c-b09723bef308", "source_id": "8f3ef2dc-d8c7-4162-9df3-2f5eed6a754d", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "waterproof_roof_standing_water — Supports treating drainage capacity/layout as a design condition, not a coating property.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "EN 12056-3 covers roof drainage layout and hydraulic calculation for gravity drainage systems.", "relevant_section_page": "Scope: roof drainage layout and calculation"}, {"id": "225a3a8b-fc53-4c52-86ff-143a0b873071", "active": true, "entity_id": "a1a3b81b-e18b-48fb-a833-99a4ef491397", "source_id": "9f413a51-501b-46b1-906e-5b6844fabddc", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "insulation_external_etics — Greek thermal-design context; does not prescribe a specific proprietary detail.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "T.O.T.E.E. 20701-2 identifies thermal bridges as local two-dimensional heat-flow discontinuities that increase losses and reduce internal surface temperature.", "relevant_section_page": "§2.4 thermal bridges"}, {"id": "1b480e90-84a8-4b37-b28d-108769a1d442", "active": true, "entity_id": "a5fa64bc-b1af-4261-b169-d0b4be268c54", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_metal_rusty — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "55697036-bf29-4a5c-b4b6-3bb3d63fb800", "active": true, "entity_id": "ac0449db-5ce6-450c-8413-c5ea08d687f8", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "repair_damaged_plaster — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "03423c7e-ff5a-4a67-88cc-b6725d343da5", "active": true, "entity_id": "b5c20d41-bfe1-4685-998e-8935773d37d3", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "waterproof_balcony_leak — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "a3e2b01d-103c-4dc3-b24d-4a89442b89d2", "active": true, "entity_id": "ba72ba99-4064-4213-9db4-0545974a706e", "source_id": "141a3e27-7aa1-41f4-9a19-7d9185385618", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_mould_damp — General health/building-moisture principle; not Greek law.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "EPA guidance says the water or moisture problem must be fixed and mould cleaned/dried; painting mouldy surfaces is not a substitute for remediation.", "relevant_section_page": "Basic mould cleanup / moisture control"}, {"id": "7166d361-e013-4e98-b156-3980fc1774ee", "active": true, "entity_id": "ba773690-d03e-4577-98b8-5fa80615580e", "source_id": "228fcd5a-dbaa-41e7-9aaf-1a9cd7266381", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_metal_rusty — Protective-coating context for steel.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "ISO 12944-4 covers types of steel surfaces and their preparation before protective paint systems.", "relevant_section_page": "Abstract / surface types and preparation"}, {"id": "8d7d91c1-60ea-446b-ae32-5aab5afa5e8f", "active": true, "entity_id": "c3440845-fb45-46af-bc49-55ce45c41fe2", "source_id": "844f5cba-66a7-4781-bb9b-ac2f5ef290ac", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "waterproof_roof_standing_water — Does not assert a universal ponding tolerance. Exact limits belong to Layer B.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "The waterproofing kit is assessed for its declared intended use and system characteristics; tolerance of actual exposure conditions must therefore be verified for the selected kit.", "relevant_section_page": "Scope / intended use of liquid-applied roof waterproofing kits"}, {"id": "fa1b815d-cf28-45a3-9e4d-6511e0639066", "active": true, "entity_id": "c3b7a958-c77f-4c53-be21-d0488430b18c", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "repair_hairline_wall_crack — Exact crack width/depth/movement limits belong to Layer B manufacturer data.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Wall repair methods vary by defect size and repair material; the selected repair compound/system determines its own application limits.", "relevant_section_page": "Small holes versus larger repairs"}, {"id": "22ffa994-d2c4-4284-94df-dccf7b5ae1fa", "active": true, "entity_id": "cc7e635a-10e1-42e6-9b67-2d7771134347", "source_id": "25f57aab-d2d3-4986-bb22-600e7268ace4", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_exterior_chalking — Supports conditional, not automatic, primer selection. Exact primer is Layer B.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "The preparation guidance separates removal of chalk from primer selection and uses primer only where needed for the resulting substrate condition.", "relevant_section_page": "Exterior surface preparation — chalk and priming"}, {"id": "e4d63616-c9e7-4d7a-b158-c0f01e41828f", "active": true, "entity_id": "d2b9c377-d789-4f0c-93bf-b53b99593cf7", "source_id": "9f413a51-501b-46b1-906e-5b6844fabddc", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_mould_damp — Greek building-physics context.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "T.O.T.E.E. 20701-2 explains that thermal bridges can lower internal surface temperature, which is relevant to surface-humidity and condensation risk.", "relevant_section_page": "§2.4 thermal bridges"}, {"id": "f772069a-50e2-4491-a114-5942bd25048e", "active": true, "entity_id": "d2d57004-85ba-465b-95ef-6aabb8da96fb", "source_id": "5779529c-513c-4ac6-989c-1727d0c3146f", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_stained — Specific stain blocker belongs to Layer B manufacturer evidence.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Stain treatment is part of coating-system selection and preparation; no universal stain-blocking primer is established for all stain causes and substrates.", "relevant_section_page": "Preparation and system-selection scope"}, {"id": "27f5e7b2-6614-4f8f-bbab-47942820db77", "active": true, "entity_id": "dacdc681-8203-4c55-80b8-3c1ed2cd6ad5", "source_id": "2ad7c061-8c16-46af-a765-590721476527", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "waterproof_balcony_leak — General balcony-system context; exact kit compatibility remains Layer B.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "LRWA describes balcony waterproofing as a system exposed to weather/traffic and highlights critical details such as supports, thresholds and rainwater outlets.", "relevant_section_page": "Balcony waterproofing — exposure and details"}, {"id": "3fe2a02b-b725-4838-9cb5-696dac2c1e7e", "active": true, "entity_id": "ded76d6d-f6fc-40da-9826-93d7a0abd423", "source_id": "8508b539-532b-476f-a1ec-068a60b91c77", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_repaint_sound — General repaint preparation.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Surface-preparation guidance requires loose, peeling and contaminating material to be removed and the surface prepared before repainting.", "relevant_section_page": "Previously painted surfaces / surface preparation"}, {"id": "6c52d7a4-ab7f-497f-8809-d62128f258b3", "active": true, "entity_id": "e15d2360-2732-4ec2-a48b-bc80d057e62d", "source_id": "5779529c-513c-4ac6-989c-1727d0c3146f", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_new_plaster — Exact Vitex primer is Layer B and must not be inferred from this general source.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Painting practice requires preparation and suitable system selection for new substrates; the exact primer and application settings depend on the selected coating system.", "relevant_section_page": "Scope: preparation and initial painting"}, {"id": "2bf9c589-70be-49f5-ab7c-db64bc59b583", "active": true, "entity_id": "e64ce745-08dc-4d36-b808-e06501197a5f", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "repair_hairline_wall_crack — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "6d899a40-9020-47cd-b847-1cef1d48522e", "active": true, "entity_id": "ed852f02-8e6a-4dc1-8824-df8f61c08963", "source_id": "25f57aab-d2d3-4986-bb22-600e7268ace4", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_exterior_chalking — General preparation principle only; no Sherwin product recommendation is imported.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Sherwin-Williams states that chalky surfaces should be cleaned to remove chalk before painting and allowed to dry.", "relevant_section_page": "Exterior surface preparation — chalky surfaces"}, {"id": "07e9e8d5-d5ad-4bbd-846c-4ff22f9d5d8f", "active": true, "entity_id": "ef07a942-f7e6-4b3b-ac06-afb907f08e1d", "source_id": "06e1dba9-9365-4a5d-8e5f-0564d4df99d3", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "insulation_internal_condensation_risk — Supports hygrothermal assessment before assuming an internal-insulation build-up is safe.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "ISO 13788 provides calculation methods concerning critical internal surface humidity and interstitial condensation in building components.", "relevant_section_page": "Scope / abstract"}, {"id": "48e78e50-3e22-4c60-8f42-c5c4e7bb62ab", "active": true, "entity_id": "fbc6ac0e-43c9-4181-8852-6e5d1dd043ba", "source_id": "5ef44a5a-f6fe-44e4-b703-6dc86e02948e", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_new_plaster — Supports why KONTA MOU must not use one universal coverage or waste factor; the selected product declaration remains the calculation basis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "Hempel distinguishes theoretical from practical consumption and states that practical consumption varies with film waviness, surface size/shape, substrate roughness and physical losses.", "relevant_section_page": "Practical consumption / Consumption Factor"}, {"id": "6af61363-2971-45e9-8e13-2f2bf6efd7c6", "active": true, "entity_id": "fbe95aa3-cce3-4efc-ada4-71dd8dc4334a", "source_id": "5779529c-513c-4ac6-989c-1727d0c3146f", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "paint_interior_repaint_sound — Exact compatibility remains a selected-system/manufacturer question.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Maintenance painting requires assessment of the existing coating/substrate before selecting a new system.", "relevant_section_page": "Maintenance painting / preparation scope"}, {"id": "dd79dc5e-27c3-4d6d-a2f1-aba843e7df37", "active": true, "entity_id": "fed03c16-3287-47ab-952e-cf5f0188f31c", "source_id": "844f5cba-66a7-4781-bb9b-ac2f5ef290ac", "created_at": "2026-09-21T09:40:57.103749+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_rule", "applicability": "waterproof_flat_roof — EU waterproofing-kit principle.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "EAD 030350-00-0402 defines liquid-applied roof waterproofing as a kit/system for the assessed intended use.", "relevant_section_page": "§1.1 scope and kit components"}, {"id": "63ede048-7631-4486-85f2-1360d7992985", "active": true, "entity_id": "0680b8e1-73ac-414f-95c3-c9d0d639a55b", "source_id": "5779529c-513c-4ac6-989c-1727d0c3146f", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Stain cause and product-specific stain-blocking behaviour are not inferred from the standard. Scenario: paint_interior_stained.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "BS 6150 provides a recognised building-painting framework in which surface condition and preparation are assessed before the decorative coating system is selected.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope / preparation framework"}, {"id": "7e1acca3-0a7d-4af5-8508-e419c8d67b4d", "active": true, "entity_id": "0a44e80f-f4c6-4c66-888a-07a892f7bf59", "source_id": "141a3e27-7aa1-41f4-9a19-7d9185385618", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General moisture/mould guidance; extensive or uncertain cases are escalated rather than diagnosed by the Studio. Scenario: paint_interior_mould_damp.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "EPA guidance makes moisture control, correction of water problems, mould cleanup and complete drying prerequisites before painting mould-affected surfaces.", "relevant_section_page": "Basic mould cleanup steps"}, {"id": "62a54d09-28e0-4f6e-866d-edb87c54b488", "active": true, "entity_id": "0b946c48-9b92-4910-b897-543452a053d8", "source_id": "8508b539-532b-476f-a1ec-068a60b91c77", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Ordinary non-structural repainting only; exact coating compatibility remains product-specific. Scenario: paint_interior_repaint_sound.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "General surface-preparation guidance requires a clean, sound and appropriately prepared existing surface before repainting.", "relevant_section_page": "Surface preparation"}, {"id": "fc03bb63-18cc-4529-88e0-47a0b54b6f43", "active": true, "entity_id": "109a8b85-995c-41e5-b8e1-fce0ca92a31f", "source_id": "8508b539-532b-476f-a1ec-068a60b91c77", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Ordinary non-structural repainting only; exact system selection remains product-specific. Scenario: paint_exterior_repaint_sound.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "General surface-preparation guidance requires surfaces to be sound, clean and suitably prepared before painting and addresses removal/preparation of unsound existing coatings.", "relevant_section_page": "Surface preparation"}, {"id": "75a35cbc-77fc-4349-b0bd-b979fb57d080", "active": true, "entity_id": "12714ce8-84ed-4255-8c3f-cf1e5328d310", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General liquid-waterproofing inspection practice; exact selected system rules remain manufacturer-specific. Scenario: waterproof_flat_roof.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "LRWA guidance requires roof inspection, safe access, substrate identification, condition assessment, leak-source investigation, moisture assessment and inspection of drainage/details before specifying a liquid-applied waterproofing system.", "relevant_section_page": "Sections 2–5, pp. 1–4"}, {"id": "b9c072db-47fb-4e2e-bb95-6183440e41b3", "active": true, "entity_id": "1427028a-cfe7-474d-b245-69d7ccde213e", "source_id": "d3d86175-0a94-4a12-93e0-3dae713325c9", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General wood-finishing principles; exact coating steps and environmental limits remain manufacturer-specific. Scenario: paint_wood_bare.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "The USDA Wood Handbook finishing chapter describes wood finishing as dependent on substrate condition, preparation, moisture/exposure and the selected finish system.", "relevant_section_page": "Wood Handbook, Chapter 16 — Finishing wood"}, {"id": "5fa5899a-ac5d-4558-ba62-f9342f64b2ab", "active": true, "entity_id": "1a25c5a4-4a34-40c8-b977-b451b18f8b74", "source_id": "8508b539-532b-476f-a1ec-068a60b91c77", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Ordinary non-structural repainting only; exact coating compatibility remains product-specific. Scenario: paint_interior_repaint_sound.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "General surface-preparation guidance requires a clean, sound and appropriately prepared existing surface before repainting.", "relevant_section_page": "Surface preparation"}, {"id": "fbd80002-48a0-4080-908c-51f0fa59ac13", "active": true, "entity_id": "1a4a509f-dbbc-4126-ad1c-7053f118c3eb", "source_id": "f3906f7a-9771-4857-b739-8d1bc8105e72", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General ETICS sequencing/system context only; exact component/product instructions remain manufacturer evidence. Scenario: insulation_external_etics.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "The EAE European Application Guideline treats ETICS as a complete system whose quality, safety and durability depend on correct system design and installation, with system-holder instructions also governing application.", "relevant_section_page": "European Application Guideline for ETICS"}, {"id": "108ede6f-baa1-40dc-99ab-37f6d4dae43c", "active": true, "entity_id": "1a93e50c-fb10-415b-93db-7cd9d714fa5d", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General liquid-waterproofing inspection practice; UK regulatory references are not treated as Greek law and exact system application remains manufacturer-specific. Scenario: waterproof_balcony_leak.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "LRWA guidance requires inspection of balcony/roof construction, substrate, membrane condition, drains, joints, cracks, flashings and other details; where leaking, the water-ingress source must be investigated before repair/specification.", "relevant_section_page": "Sections 3–5, pp. 2–4"}, {"id": "ef543fd9-88ac-43ba-8779-2263242e8f44", "active": true, "entity_id": "1ad6702f-f72c-46