age/falls principle; does not establish a product-specific tolerance for ponding. Scenario: waterproof_roof_standing_water.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "LRWA flat-roof falls guidance treats falls and drainage as core design/maintenance considerations where ponding occurs.", "relevant_section_page": "Guidance Note No. 7 — flat roof falls"}, {"id": "061858c2-cd90-4824-b7e7-0652d1dbef56", "active": true, "entity_id": "354def21-b2c5-4488-a775-99cfeb10c722", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General liquid-waterproofing inspection practice; UK regulatory references are not treated as Greek law and exact system application remains manufacturer-specific. Scenario: waterproof_balcony_leak.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "LRWA guidance requires inspection of balcony/roof construction, substrate, membrane condition, drains, joints, cracks, flashings and other details; where leaking, the water-ingress source must be investigated before repair/specification.", "relevant_section_page": "Sections 3–5, pp. 2–4"}, {"id": "8dd54100-171d-4885-a112-cd784f5d9151", "active": true, "entity_id": "3c9f132c-b382-4484-97b1-473b3701420d", "source_id": "d3d86175-0a94-4a12-93e0-3dae713325c9", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General wood-finishing principles; exact coating steps and environmental limits remain manufacturer-specific. Scenario: paint_wood_bare.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "The USDA Wood Handbook finishing chapter describes wood finishing as dependent on substrate condition, preparation, moisture/exposure and the selected finish system.", "relevant_section_page": "Wood Handbook, Chapter 16 — Finishing wood"}, {"id": "1bb2a406-0aa9-4d21-97f4-52d821613473", "active": true, "entity_id":