ct coating compatibility remains product-specific. Scenario: paint_interior_repaint_sound.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "General surface-preparation guidance requires a clean, sound and appropriately prepared existing surface before repainting.", "relevant_section_page": "Surface preparation"}, {"id": "dd6c2414-b056-4134-ba9c-1c34a1ad76e9", "active": true, "entity_id": "e1a07ded-13d6-4d46-b33e-7052a95b840c", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General liquid-waterproofing inspection practice; exact selected system rules remain manufacturer-specific. Scenario: waterproof_flat_roof.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "LRWA guidance requires roof inspection, safe access, substrate identification, condition assessment, leak-source investigation, moisture assessment and inspection of drainage/details before specifying a liquid-applied waterproofing system.", "relevant_section_page": "Sections 2–5, pp. 1–4"}, {"id": "71b0d3ee-9f52-4bbc-98b9-a238e73f6b33", "active": true, "entity_id": "ec608036-78b5-4f56-85f7-f7ddbf359f30", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General liquid-waterproofing inspection practice; exact selected system rules remain manufacturer-specific. Scenario: waterproof_flat_roof.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "LRWA guidance requires roof inspection, safe access, substrate identification, condition assessment, leak-source investigation, moisture assessment and inspection of drainage/details before specifying a liquid-applied waterproofing system.", "relevant_section_page": "Sections 2–5, pp. 1–4"}, {"id": "e94d06ea-bccb-483a-8be0-28bf15e4b792", "active": true, "entity_id": "ee56533a-374d-4e11-8ee4-c4b10a9ec0ed", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General liquid-waterproofing inspection practice; UK regulatory references are not treated as Greek law and exact system application remains manufacturer-specific. Scenario: waterproof_balcony_leak.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "LRWA guidance requires inspection of balcony/roof construction, substrate, membrane condition, drains, joints, cracks, flashings and other details; where leaking, the water-ingress source must be investigated before repair/specification.", "relevant_section_page": "Sections 3–5, pp. 2–4"}, {"id": "20b65780-0f6e-4481-8087-6b7f3de96a06", "active": true, "entity_id": "eebf312d-d0d9-49d2-aa17-d3a2e5402be4", "source_id": "141a3e27-7aa1-41f4-9a19-7d9185385618", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General moisture/mould guidance; extensive or uncertain cases are escalated rather than diagnosed by the Studio. Scenario: paint_interior_mould_damp.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "EPA guidance makes moisture control, correction of water problems, mould cleanup and complete drying prerequisites before painting mould-affected surfaces.", "relevant_section_page": "Basic mould cleanup steps"}, {"id": "244b967d-ea50-41e6-bcc1-186db6930139", "active": true, "entity_id": "ef5e0842-cdb8-4b6a-a425-7edc59c9901c", "source_id": "228fcd5a-dbaa-41e7-9aaf-1a9cd7266381", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General steel-preparation principle; exact preparation grade and coating system depend on the project/product specification. Scenario: paint_metal_rusty.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "ISO 12944-4 addresses surface types and preparation of steel surfaces for corrosion-protective paint systems, supporting removal/preparation of corrosion and contaminants before coating.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope"}, {"id": "55eda0c1-8c31-478e-b759-773a3c29be1e", "active": true, "entity_id": "f09d0e64-fcb9-458e-9d07-3dae20f4d1d0", "source_id": "5779529c-513c-4ac6-989c-1727d0c3146f", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Stain cause and product-specific stain-blocking behaviour are not inferred from the standard. Scenario: paint_interior_stained.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "BS 6150 provides a recognised building-painting framework in which surface condition and preparation are assessed before the decorative coating system is selected.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope / preparation framework"}, {"id": "7fd0efb3-f69b-4b1f-832a-30e2f59c3ef0", "active": true, "entity_id": "f09ec731-2666-4c8c-a6cf-31fafea4791a", "source_id": "3829ce05-0552-4545-84f5-f4ecb76bb00a", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Internal truth-layer governance for a step that explicitly depends on the selected product/manufacturer.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "KONTA MOU governance requires exact product application limits, cure/readiness, primers, coat counts and other manufacturer-specific instructions to come from verified manufacturer evidence, not the general guidance layer.", "relevant_section_page": "Manufacturer-boundary rule"}, {"id": "262d0c13-4131-4ab9-b613-a8dce427a175", "active": true, "entity_id": "f09ec731-2666-4c8c-a6cf-31fafea4791a", "source_id": "f3906f7a-9771-4857-b739-8d1bc8105e72", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General ETICS sequencing/system context only; exact component/product instructions remain manufacturer evidence. Scenario: insulation_external_etics.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "The EAE European Application Guideline treats ETICS as a complete system whose quality, safety and durability depend on correct system design and installation, with system-holder instructions also governing application.", "relevant_section_page": "European Application Guideline for ETICS"}, {"id": "3a70cbc5-6bd9-410f-800e-eb0f968b89cc", "active": true, "entity_id": "f19844ea-eb9a-4352-ae12-8db2726bd159", "source_id": "3829ce05-0552-4545-84f5-f4ecb76bb00a", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Internal truth-layer governance for a step that explicitly depends on the selected product/manufacturer.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "KONTA MOU governance requires exact product application limits, cure/readiness, primers, coat counts and other manufacturer-specific instructions to come from verified manufacturer evidence, not the general guidance layer.", "relevant_section_page": "Manufacturer-boundary rule"}, {"id": "14c66b93-c836-4809-bd65-9cba60ab9194", "active": true, "entity_id": "f19844ea-eb9a-4352-ae12-8db2726bd159", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Ordinary non-structural wall repair only; widespread failure, moisture or structural indications require escalation. Scenario: repair_damaged_plaster.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Professional wall-repair guidance removes loose/flaking material, repairs the substrate, allows repair material to dry, and prepares the repaired area before finishing.", "relevant_section_page": "Wall repair — preparation and patching"}, {"id": "006d7ead-deb2-4836-a341-4c450e6ba14f", "active": true, "entity_id": "f33580d4-97ed-4b85-99ab-a851e767e5f5", "source_id": "c5efac2e-3bde-47b7-90d4-27341236d3c8", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Conservative crack screening only; no UK numerical threshold is used as a universal Greek rule. Scenario: paint_exterior_hairline_cracks.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "RICS notes that visible cracks can require measurement/monitoring and that new or expanding cracks and other movement indicators warrant further investigation rather than automatic cosmetic treatment.", "relevant_section_page": "How can I tell if my house is subsiding?"}, {"id": "3438aa94-7f79-434f-a114-cfb5509dc0e2", "active": true, "entity_id": "f5d0bf41-3129-4895-8338-91049c71f63a", "source_id": "228fcd5a-dbaa-41e7-9aaf-1a9cd7266381", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General steel-preparation principle; exact preparation grade and coating system depend on the project/product specification. Scenario: paint_metal_rusty.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "ISO 12944-4 addresses surface types and preparation of steel surfaces for corrosion-protective paint systems, supporting removal/preparation of corrosion and contaminants before coating.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope"}, {"id": "79e85786-2063-4ad3-b4d7-50e0032ed1e9", "active": true, "entity_id": "f6c0899a-c017-4735-b53b-ed61ba6120e9", "source_id": "228fcd5a-dbaa-41e7-9aaf-1a9cd7266381", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General steel-preparation principle; exact preparation grade and coating system depend on the project/product specification. Scenario: paint_metal_rusty.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "ISO 12944-4 addresses surface types and preparation of steel surfaces for corrosion-protective paint systems, supporting removal/preparation of corrosion and contaminants before coating.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope"}, {"id": "c85c4ced-a520-4345-bf44-5c8d7402d6dc", "active": true, "entity_id": "f90acad4-3157-4190-b1b4-e76f3b075613", "source_id": "d3d86175-0a94-4a12-93e0-3dae713325c9", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General wood-finishing principles; exact coating steps and environmental limits remain manufacturer-specific. Scenario: paint_wood_bare.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "The USDA Wood Handbook finishing chapter describes wood finishing as dependent on substrate condition, preparation, moisture/exposure and the selected finish system.", "relevant_section_page": "Wood Handbook, Chapter 16 — Finishing wood"}, {"id": "cdbd5a10-99c4-401a-8031-6979484d0816", "active": true, "entity_id": "f9afb542-4826-441e-abc5-34d87c4a8755", "source_id": "06e1dba9-9365-4a5d-8e5f-0564d4df99d3", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General hygrothermal risk screening; detailed design may require a more complete assessment than ISO 13788 alone. Scenario: insulation_internal_condensation_risk.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "ISO 13788 provides methods to assess internal surface conditions associated with critical surface humidity and interstitial condensation, supporting condensation-risk assessment before selecting an internal-insulation solution.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope"}, {"id": "31b4a403-86ce-4dc6-bf95-ef9da7b47624", "active": true, "entity_id": "fa524c14-5556-4c30-bf80-f7be7be71a35", "source_id": "228fcd5a-dbaa-41e7-9aaf-1a9cd7266381", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "General steel-preparation principle; exact preparation grade and coating system depend on the project/product specification. Scenario: paint_metal_rusty.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "ISO 12944-4 addresses surface types and preparation of steel surfaces for corrosion-protective paint systems, supporting removal/preparation of corrosion and contaminants before coating.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope"}, {"id": "8957371d-ae96-49b8-8622-593d7066686d", "active": true, "entity_id": "fcaf3a07-ef6f-408c-9e04-4f161afea55e", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:18:58.0713+00:00", "entity_type": "solution_step", "applicability": "Ordinary non-structural wall repair only; widespread failure, moisture or structural indications require escalation. Scenario: repair_damaged_plaster.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "Professional wall-repair guidance removes loose/flaking material, repairs the substrate, allows repair material to dry, and prepares the repaired area before finishing.", "relevant_section_page": "Wall repair — preparation and patching"}, {"id": "7c41ed2c-5d1b-445c-8a12-02ac6e0506bb", "active": true, "entity_id": "1f1169e1-1dec-4974-a517-95196ebdce0d", "source_id": "8508b539-532b-476f-a1ec-068a60b91c77", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "General coating-preparation principle for ordinary non-structural substrates.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "General painting preparation guidance requires loose, peeling or otherwise unsound material to be removed and the surface made sound before coating.", "relevant_section_page": "Surface preparation"}, {"id": "82ae5e25-93e4-41fc-886a-dbab38106b02", "active": true, "entity_id": "20229d2a-637e-4a32-a443-e28d2f4cca62", "source_id": "3829ce05-0552-4545-84f5-f4ecb76bb00a", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Internal workflow/safety rule.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "KONTA MOU safety governance escalates widespread detached or falling material because the Studio must not treat a potentially hazardous substrate as a cosmetic paint defect.", "relevant_section_page": "Safety escalation rules"}, {"id": "894f0a37-4f59-49c0-b8af-66273143ee66", "active": true, "entity_id": "20229d2a-637e-4a32-a443-e28d2f4cca62", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Supports the unstable-material principle; KONTA MOU adds professional escalation for widespread/falling material as a conservative safety rule.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Wall-repair guidance removes loose/flaking material before repair and finishing rather than concealing unstable material under filler or paint.", "relevant_section_page": "Wall repair / scraping and preparation"}, {"id": "08be21f0-bce5-460a-a67b-fcea8007f326", "active": true, "entity_id": "4d69e36b-4cef-46ad-9df8-a859195c5d61", "source_id": "b4b2697f-66a3-41d2-a8a9-2c2a67161f02", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Supports checking drainage/falls before recommending a waterproof coating for standing-water situations.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "LRWA flat-roof falls guidance treats drainage and falls as part of roof design and ponding control rather than something a coating alone can be assumed to correct.", "relevant_section_page": "Flat roof falls / drainage guidance"}, {"id": "0be34536-4214-4054-9124-316cb6e647a3", "active": true, "entity_id": "4e1b7b67-05d9-4017-a5da-80ab7f3b15cb", "source_id": "d05944ec-a82c-47a1-953c-6ff28e5bd801", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "EU occupational-safety context; used as a KONTA MOU DIY stop rule, not as a substitute for site-specific legal compliance assessment.", "evidence_strength": "regulatory", "supporting_passage": "EU-OSHA guidance treats work at height as a fall-risk activity requiring risk assessment and prevention/protection measures before work proceeds.", "relevant_section_page": "Working at height — risk prevention"}, {"id": "b5ed859f-b59d-4a7a-a36e-8724520f6422", "active": true, "entity_id": "5d1ac767-6ffb-4b4a-a3f3-6b0a70d87f75", "source_id": "8508b539-532b-476f-a1ec-068a60b91c77", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Supports a test/verification pathway where an existing coating is not confidently identified as compatible.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "General surface-preparation guidance requires the existing surface/coating condition to be assessed and prepared for adhesion; uncertain compatibility should not be assumed across the full project.", "relevant_section_page": "Surface preparation / adhesion"}, {"id": "356b21ae-cedb-4cf1-835e-e9a1dbbac829", "active": true, "entity_id": "7348e5a3-d600-4c23-a3a6-036ef747183d", "source_id": "141a3e27-7aa1-41f4-9a19-7d9185385618", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "General moisture/mould safety guidance; not presented as Greek building law.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "EPA mould guidance makes moisture control and correction of the water problem a prerequisite to durable mould cleanup and states that mouldy surfaces should not simply be painted over.", "relevant_section_page": "Basic mould cleanup steps"}, {"id": "cbc66b00-8da9-4a22-a71c-ad14535f66b7", "active": true, "entity_id": "76300706-1165-4fc9-ae90-79a966706c1f", "source_id": "3829ce05-0552-4545-84f5-f4ecb76bb00a", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Internal safety boundary; it intentionally avoids making a structural diagnosis.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "KONTA MOU safety governance blocks cosmetic repair guidance where observations may involve a structural element and requires professional assessment instead of inferring structural condition.", "relevant_section_page": "Structural-risk stop rule"}, {"id": "19490a8d-d2ab-4aa1-929b-d8f8707a513d", "active": true, "entity_id": "7ad84cc3-fa41-44aa-8f32-790a26cdbaf2", "source_id": "06e1dba9-9365-4a5d-8e5f-0564d4df99d3", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Applies specifically to condensation-risk differentiation, not to diagnosing every moisture source.", "evidence_strength": "standard_based", "supporting_passage": "ISO 13788 provides calculation methods for internal surface humidity and interstitial condensation, demonstrating that condensation is a distinct hygrothermal mechanism requiring assessment rather than visual assumption.", "relevant_section_page": "Standard scope"}, {"id": "0c9e522f-4821-4e97-bece-b5416f3668fd", "active": true, "entity_id": "7ad84cc3-fa41-44aa-8f32-790a26cdbaf2", "source_id": "5efe64a0-4dea-44a6-a662-0aeaba6fcbe9", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Supports uncertainty handling when the source of significant moisture is not established.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "RICS damp-and-mould guidance distinguishes multiple potential moisture mechanisms and supports investigation of the cause rather than assuming one source from appearance alone.", "relevant_section_page": "Damp and mould — causes / diagnosis"}, {"id": "c04ea655-9209-4dcf-8788-a6a48ed76cf5", "active": true, "entity_id": "87863b47-9fce-47c6-88c0-1ed01a2c1074", "source_id": "34563425-ac2b-4a6c-89f2-8bc4090678de", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "KONTA_MOU_RULE — Supports blocking coating-only advice while active ingress source/path remains unresolved.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "LRWA inspection guidance states that when a roof, balcony or walkway is already leaking, the source of water ingress must be determined and defects in the membrane, deck, details or flashings identified for repair or replacement.", "relevant_section_page": "Section 4 Condition, p. 3"}, {"id": "87bd541a-e3af-42ae-889c-d4b9758aec86", "active": true, "entity_id": "a05b1f67-9e42-4004-85a4-7e7691b9649d", "source_id": "3829ce05-0552-4545-84f5-f4ecb76bb00a", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Internal decision-safety governance; does not claim an external construction requirement.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "KONTA MOU governance keeps general guidance, manufacturer instructions and platform safety rules as separate truth layers and requires conflicts to be surfaced rather than silently reconciled.", "relevant_section_page": "Truth-layer governance"}, {"id": "fe225341-8f35-4296-81a8-8c9a648f9a02", "active": true, "entity_id": "cfcbe420-ed6d-4290-b8ab-12215299f2bb", "source_id": "3829ce05-0552-4545-84f5-f4ecb76bb00a", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "Internal decision-safety governance preventing invented product instructions.", "evidence_strength": "strong_consensus", "supporting_passage": "KONTA MOU governance assigns exact dilution, coat count, consumption, recoat/cure times and product limits to verified manufacturer evidence rather than the general layer.", "relevant_section_page": "Manufacturer-boundary rule"}, {"id": "a6f77892-3e85-456f-bd8d-3b60ca862669", "active": true, "entity_id": "d70d6b88-e01b-4af9-9c8d-3eb9f234cc5b", "source_id": "c5efac2e-3bde-47b7-90d4-27341236d3c8", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:17:16.52662+00:00", "entity_type": "stop_condition", "applicability": "General conservative screening only; no UK numerical crack threshold is used as a Greek rule.", "evidence_strength": "context_dependent", "supporting_passage": "RICS identifies new or expanding cracks and other movement indicators as reasons for further investigation/specialist help rather than treating the crack as a purely cosmetic defect.", "relevant_section_page": "How can I tell if my house is subsiding?"}, {"id": "d4c11d7a-87d4-45ef-ba21-75cf63ce270f", "active": true, "entity_id": "02009d2c-46e9-4bd5-8eb3-6299b2dc762e", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:21:22.404499+00:00", "entity_type": "tool_requirement", "applicability": "Only after crack stability screening; exact repair method remains product-specific. Scenario: repair_hairline_wall_crack.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Wall-repair guidance covers scraping/preparation, filling, smoothing/sanding and cleanup operations for ordinary non-structural wall repairs.", "relevant_section_page": "Wall repair — preparation and patching"}, {"id": "fc4283c9-8aa9-4c91-8e15-50e2de436a18", "active": true, "entity_id": "057d5f4a-c073-458d-bf0d-a1cffc2df5c5", "source_id": "72337f4f-0492-4ac7-ad0a-424770c4bc11", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:21:22.404499+00:00", "entity_type": "tool_requirement", "applicability": "General non-structural repair tool categories only; crack diagnosis remains separate. Scenario: paint_exterior_hairline_cracks.", "evidence_strength": "common_professional_practice", "supporting_passage": "Wall-repair guidance uses common scraping, filling, smoothing/sanding and cleanup operations before repainting.", "relevant_section_page": "Wall repair — preparation and patching"}, {"id": "7081078d-9a60-4298-a07f-0dc3e74924e0", "active": true, "entity_id": "0d83b966-52fc-4c30-9890-0050a25294ed", "source_id": "0211758f-174c-4fbb-b17a-2a374fa64327", "created_at": "2026-09-21T10:21:22.404499+00:00", "entity_type": "tool_requirement", "applicability": "General tool-category guidance only. Scenario: paint_interior_new_plaster.", "evidence_strength": "common_profe